  $ cat > /tmp/claude-1000/-home-grymmjack-git-qb64/8aae2dea-6211-45f1-bf59-216af8899b42/scratchpad/newblock.bm <<'EOF'
  $     ''
  $     ' Load a PC speaker sound bank. Returns TRUE on success. Understands:
  $     '   - Duke Nukem 1 / Commander Keen IFS banks ("SND",0 header), and IFS
  $     '     banks inside a bigger file (Cosmo's COSMO?.STN, Major Stryker's
  $     '     VOLUME?A.MS?) - every bank in the file is loaded
  $     '   - DOOM engine WADs (IWAD / PWAD): every DP* lump becomes one sound,
  $     '     and so does every lump between PCSTART and PCSTOP (Rise of the
  $     '     Triad)
  $     '   - a single DOOM PC speaker lump on its own (e.g. DPPISTOL.LMP)
  $     '   - id Software AUDIOHED.* / AUDIOT.* pairs - pass either one
  $     '   - Duke Nukem II's NUKEM2.CMP (it holds AUDIOHED.MNI and AUDIOT.MNI)
  $     '   - Crystal Caves' CC?-?.SND raw divisor lists
  $     ' Whatever the source, the sounds end up as PIT divisors at 140 Hz, so
  $     ' all the PCSPK_IFS* calls below work the same for every kind.
